     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Answers may vary.\n<ul>\n<li>The total number of vertices in each graph is different. The Diamonds graph has 17 vertices while Dots graph has only 16.</li>\n<li>The degrees of vertices differ. The Diamonds graph has vertices of degrees 4 while the Dots graph does not.</li>\n<li>The graphs have different sizes of cyclic subgraphs. The Diamonds graph has 4 squares (4-cycles), while the Dots graph has 3 squares.  Also, the Dots graph has 8-cycles while the Diamonds graph does not.</li>\n</ul>"
    }
